Layout: three full-body views of the same child, side by side, evenly spaced and at the same scale, on a plain, evenly lit, very light cream background:
1. Front view: standing, facing the viewer, gentle smile, arms relaxed, both feet pointing toward the viewer.
2. Three-quarter view turned toward the viewer's left: the face, eyes, chest, hips and both feet all turn toward the left side of the picture; waving with one raised hand.
3. Side view in full profile facing the viewer's left, walking to the left: the nose and eyes, the chest, the swinging arms, the knees and the toes of both shoes all point to the left side of the picture.
Each figure is one body turned one way: the head never looks the other way from the body and feet.
Each view shows the whole child, from the top of the head to the soles of both shoes, with a clear band of empty background below the shoes and above the head: no part of any view touches or runs off the edge of the picture. The shoes are fully visible, each with a clear, darker outline and sole, light-colored shoes too, so they stand out from the background and from the soft floor shadow.
